# Docker build context for the ingest image (deploy/ingest.Dockerfile). An allowlist, like
# /.dockerignore: everything is excluded, then only what the image is built from is let back
# in. Docker uses this file instead of /.dockerignore for that Dockerfile, so the web image's
# context is unchanged.
#
# Never in the context: generated releases and the store (var/), v1's own files that hold
# FRED- and Yahoo-sourced values (data/, dist/, web/, .git), the fixtures, and v1's
# hand-entered tables inside the atlas package (the four .yaml files; the ingest job publishes
# from the store and never runs the legacy converter). tests/v2/test_ignore_rules.py checks
# this file. Do not add those paths here (build protocol, point 7).
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!atlas
!schema
!checks/spot.json
!packages/core/package.json
!packages/core/bin
!packages/core/src

atlas/approval.yaml
atlas/catalog.yaml
atlas/events.yaml
atlas/politics.yaml
**/__pycache__
**/*.test.ts
packages/core/src/testing.ts
**/node_modules
**/.env
**/.env.local
